---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import "../styles/tokens.css";
import "../styles/shell.css";
import "../styles/doc.css";
import "../styles/page.css";
---
<Base
  title={"Brand · Rabta"}
  description={"The Rabta mark: an R whose leg is the Arabic ر of رابطة. Where it comes from, how it moves, the colours it lives in, and the files to use it."}
  route="/brand/"
  ogTitle={"The Rabta mark"}
  ogDescription={"An R that is also a ر. The mark, its three strokes, its colours, and the files to use it."}
>
  <div class="wrap page-head">
    <p class="page-head__label">Brand</p>
    <h1>An R that is also a ر.</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Two alphabets, one glyph, three strokes. This page is the mark: where
      it comes from, how it moves, the colours it lives in, and the files to
      use it.
    </p>
  </div>

  <!-- The living mark. Each plate draws itself when it scrolls into view and
       again on request. -->
  <section class="band" aria-labelledby="mark-title">
    <div class="band__inner">
      <div class="band__body">
        <h2 id="mark-title">Three strokes, in the order the product happens.</h2>
        <p>
          The stem: you start a task, and something comes down to rest. The
          bowl: you capture, and the loop closes around what is open. The leg:
          you leave, and you come back. That third stroke is the Arabic ر of
          رابطة, and it is the one that gets the colour.
        </p>

        <div class="specimen">
          <div class="specimen__plate">
            <svg class="mark" id="specimen-ink" data-mark="draw" viewBox="0 0 100 100" role="img" aria-label="The Rabta mark on ink">
              <g transform="translate(4.5,-5)" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="12" stroke-linejoin="round">
                <path class="stem" d="M25 22V84" />
                <path class="bowl" d="M25 28H46a16 16 0 0 1 0 32H25" />
                <path class="leg" d="M44 60c14 4 22 10 22 16 0 5-6 8-13 6" />
              </g>
            </svg>
            <button class="button button--small specimen__replay" type="button" data-mark-replay aria-controls="specimen-ink">Draw it again</button>
          </div>
          <div class="specimen__plate specimen__plate--paper paper">
            <svg class="mark" id="specimen-paper" data-mark="draw" viewBox="0 0 100 100" role="img" aria-label="The Rabta mark on paper">
              <g transform="translate(4.5,-5)" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="12" stroke-linejoin="round">
                <path class="stem" d="M25 22V84" />
                <path class="bowl" d="M25 28H46a16 16 0 0 1 0 32H25" />
                <path class="leg" d="M44 60c14 4 22 10 22 16 0 5-6 8-13 6" />
              </g>
            </svg>
            <button class="button button--small specimen__replay" type="button" data-mark-replay aria-controls="specimen-paper">Draw it again</button>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="strokes">
          <div class="stroke" data-reveal>
            <svg class="mark" viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true">
              <g transform="translate(4.5,-5)" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="12" stroke-linejoin="round">
                <path class="stem lit" d="M25 22V84" />
                <path class="bowl" d="M25 28H46a16 16 0 0 1 0 32H25" />
                <path class="leg" d="M44 60c14 4 22 10 22 16 0 5-6 8-13 6" />
              </g>
            </svg>
            <h3>The stem</h3>
            <p>You start. A task is a name for the thing you are doing, and something comes down to rest.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="stroke" data-reveal data-reveal-delay="80">
            <svg class="mark" viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true">
              <g transform="translate(4.5,-5)" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="12" stroke-linejoin="round">
                <path class="stem" d="M25 22V84" />
                <path class="bowl lit" d="M25 28H46a16 16 0 0 1 0 32H25" />
                <path class="leg" d="M44 60c14 4 22 10 22 16 0 5-6 8-13 6" />
              </g>
            </svg>
            <h3>The bowl</h3>
            <p>You capture. The loop closes around the files, the terminals, the tabs and the branch.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="stroke" data-reveal data-reveal-delay="160">
            <svg class="mark" viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true">
              <g transform="translate(4.5,-5)" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="12" stroke-linejoin="round">
                <path class="stem" d="M25 22V84" />
                <path class="bowl" d="M25 28H46a16 16 0 0 1 0 32H25" />
                <path class="leg lit" d="M44 60c14 4 22 10 22 16 0 5-6 8-13 6" />
              </g>
            </svg>
            <h3>The leg</h3>
            <p>You leave, and you come back. The stroke goes out and returns. This is the ر, and this is the brand.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="band" aria-labelledby="name-title">
    <div class="band__inner">
      <div class="band__body">
        <h2 id="name-title">Rabta is رابطة: a bond, a link, the thing that ties things together.</h2>
        <p>
          The product is exactly that. Your tools each remember their own piece
          of a task; Rabta is the bond between them. The name is pronounced
          RAHB-tah, and it is written in the two alphabets the mark carries.
        </p>
        <div class="name" aria-hidden="true">
          <div>
            <p class="name__word">Rabta</p>
            <p>Set in Inter, weight 560, the face of everything else on this site.</p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <p class="name__word name__word--arabic">رابطة</p>
            <p>The ر is the second letter, and it is the leg of the mark. Set in Reem Kufi, a geometric Kufi whose strokes share the mark's logic.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <p class="mono muted foot-note">
          Three faces on this site, all under the SIL Open Font License and
          each shipped beside its licence: Inter for everything, Reem Kufi for
          the name only, Geist Mono for what is checkable: receipts,
          terminals, code, hashes, paths.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="band" aria-labelledby="lockup-title">
    <div class="band__inner">
      <div class="band__body">
        <h2 id="lockup-title">The mark, then the rest of the word.</h2>
        <p>
          The R's stem is scaled to Inter's cap height, so the mark and the
          letters after it share a cap line. The wordmark ships as outlines and
          never depends on a font being installed. Clear space around the
          lockup is one stem-width; the smallest it should ever be set is 22px
          tall, and the tile should never go below 16px.
        </p>
        <div class="construction" data-reveal>
          <img src="/assets/brand/lockup.svg" width="2945" height="1213" alt="The Rabta lockup: the mark followed by the letters a, b, t, a, with the leg of the R in ember orange." />
          <p>Never outline the mark, rotate it, put it in a circle, add a shadow, or draw the leg in anything but the ember or the mark's own colour.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="band" aria-labelledby="ways-title">
    <div class="band__inner">
      <div class="band__body">
        <h2 id="ways-title">Paper, ink, and the tile.</h2>
        <p>
          Two-tone is the default on paper and on ink: the stem and bowl in the
          text colour, the leg in the ember. The tile is the mark in ink on an
          ember squircle, for the Dock, the favicon and any avatar. Mono is for
          the places two colours are not available.
        </p>
        <div class="ways">
          <div class="way" data-reveal>
            <div class="way__plate way__plate--paper"><img class="way__lockup" src="/assets/brand/lockup.svg" width="2945" height="1213" alt="" /></div>
            <h3>Lockup on paper</h3>
            <a class="link link--arrow" href="/assets/brand/lockup.svg" download>Download SVG</a>
          </div>
          <div class="way" data-reveal data-reveal-delay="60">
            <div class="way__plate way__plate--ink"><img class="way__lockup" src="/assets/brand/lockup-paper.svg" width="2945" height="1213" alt="" /></div>
            <h3>Lockup on ink</h3>
            <a class="link link--arrow" href="/assets/brand/lockup-paper.svg" download>Download SVG</a>
          </div>
          <div class="way" data-reveal data-reveal-delay="120">
            <div class="way__plate way__plate--paper"><img src="/assets/brand/rabta-mark.svg" width="100" height="100" alt="" /></div>
            <h3>The tile</h3>
            <a class="link link--arrow" href="/assets/brand/icon-512.png" download>Download PNG</a>
          </div>
          <div class="way" data-reveal data-reveal-delay="180">
            <div class="way__plate way__plate--paper"><img src="/assets/brand/rabta-mark-primary.svg" width="100" height="100" alt="" /></div>
            <h3>The mark alone</h3>
            <a class="link link--arrow" href="/assets/brand/mark.svg" download>Download SVG</a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="band" aria-labelledby="palette-title">
    <div class="band__inner">
      <div class="band__body">
        <h2 id="palette-title">Paper, ink, one ember.</h2>
        <p>
          Both worlds are neutral with a cool cast, so a screenshot of the dark
          app sits naturally on the light site. The ember is spent once per
          view: on the primary action, or on the live thing, never both.
        </p>
        <div class="swatches">
          <div class="swatch" data-reveal><div class="swatch__color swatch__color--paper-0"></div><div class="swatch__meta"><b>Paper</b><span>#FFFFFF</span></div></div>
          <div class="swatch" data-reveal data-reveal-delay="40"><div class="swatch__color swatch__color--paper-1"></div><div class="swatch__meta"><b>Paper, alt</b><span>#F5F5F7</span></div></div>
          <div class="swatch" data-reveal data-reveal-delay="80"><div class="swatch__color swatch__color--ink-0"></div><div class="swatch__meta"><b>Ink</b><span>#0A0B0E</span></div></div>
          <div class="swatch" data-reveal data-reveal-delay="120"><div class="swatch__color swatch__color--ink-1"></div><div class="swatch__meta"><b>Ink, raised</b><span>#14161B</span></div></div>
          <div class="swatch" data-reveal data-reveal-delay="160"><div class="swatch__color swatch__color--ember"></div><div class="swatch__meta"><b>Ember</b><span>#FF6B2C</span></div></div>
          <div class="swatch" data-reveal data-reveal-delay="200"><div class="swatch__color swatch__color--ember-deep"></div><div class="swatch__meta"><b>Ember, deep</b><span>#C2501B</span></div></div>
          <div class="swatch" data-reveal data-reveal-delay="240"><div class="swatch__color swatch__color--text"></div><div class="swatch__meta"><b>Text</b><span>#0E0F12</span></div></div>
          <div class="swatch" data-reveal data-reveal-delay="280"><div class="swatch__color swatch__color--text-mute"></div><div class="swatch__meta"><b>Text, muted</b><span>#4A4D57</span></div></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="band band--close" aria-labelledby="motion-title">
    <div class="band__inner">
      <div class="band__body">
        <h2 id="motion-title">Everything that comes back moves the way the leg does.</h2>
        <p>
          One settling curve for anything that comes to rest, and one spring
          for the moment something lands. The mark draws itself in just over a
          second, stem first, leg last. A window returns by rising into place;
          a headline rises from behind its own baseline; a restore completes
          with the ember. Under reduced motion, all of it collapses to a fade,
          and the mark is simply there.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
